      "response": "## Investigation report\n\nCitation integrity checked against saved evidence. Human review is required to assess the findings.\n\n### 1. Docs · Low\n\nThe code imports the Streamlit library as the alias \\`st\\`\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_036e205ee1d08d9df9c4c83a6d819f45\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 2. Docs · Low\n\nThe function \\`load\\_rows\\` is decorated with \\`@st\\.cache\\_data\\`\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_036e205ee1d08d9df9c4c83a6d819f45\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 3. Docs · Low\n\n\\`load\\_rows\\` returns a static list \\`\\[1, 2, 3\\]\\`\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_036e205ee1d08d9df9c4c83a6d819f45\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 4. Docs · Low\n\nThe script calls \\`st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\\` to display the list\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_036e205ee1d08d9df9c4c83a6d819f45\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### Missing information\n\n- Runtime logs or a counter variable to confirm the caching behavior of \\`@st\\.cache\\_data\\`\\.\n\n### Proposed next steps\n\n- Perform a focused check that the cached function \\`load\\_rows\\` is executed only once per Streamlit rerun by adding a side‑effect \\(e\\.g\\., incrementing a counter\\) and verifying the counter does not increase on subsequent renders\\.\n",
